1
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:10,470
A solver reports success.

2
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:13,930
But has the physical objective met the target accuracy?

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,980
Reflections can polarize light.

4
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:21,380
A rotating polarizer changes the transmitted brightness.

5
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:24,980
Stokes coordinates describe the polarization state.

6
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,220
The smooth Stokes map keeps estimates physical.

7
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:34,500
At full linear polarization, its fold hides one physical-gradient component from first derivatives.

8
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:45,090
At the exact fold, first derivatives plus one signed radial second derivative recover the physical gradient.

9
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:51,190
This holds for objectives with continuous second derivatives, even at nonstationary points,

10
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:53,090
without knowing the physical Hessian.

11
00:00:54,950 --> 00:01:01,930
In this saved noisy reflection simulation, the raw warm start reports success at an inaccurate endpoint.

12
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:04,530
The marked gap exceeds the target.

13
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:09,670
Both audited branches are below the target gap here, following earlier restarts.

14
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:17,920
Selected by the largest baseline gap, this is not a typical scene.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,180
Dashed curves show noise-free polarization truth.

16
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:25,480
The gap measures optimization error for the noisy fitting objective.

17
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:32,730
Under strong convexity, bounded intensity, and all inner-sheet theorem conditions,

18
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:37,890
the displayed derivative and curvature tolerances bound the objective gap.

19
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:40,810
Stop when this upper bound meets the target.

20
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,990
The guarantees are conditional.

21
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:49,430
Real-data failures extend beyond the local fold gate.

22
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:53,970
Direct physical solvers were cheaper in our tested implementation.

23
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:59,670
Recover what first derivatives hide. Bound the remaining objective gap.

24
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:01,750
Decide whether stopping is justified.

25
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:04,970
The contribution is information for assessing convergence.
